# /**
#  * @file .gitignore
#  * @description Git ignore rules for the Agentic Pitch Generator workspace.
#  *
#  * Why: Prevents transient Python bytecode, virtual environments, local environment
#  * secrets, Terraform state files, and CLI-generated image artifacts from polluting
#  * version control while preserving tracked templates (`.env.example`) and reference
#  * solutions (`.agents/`).
#  */

# /**
#  * Why: Exclude compiled Python bytecode and packaging metadata generated during
#  * local execution, editable installs (`pip install -e .`), and test runs so
#  * interpreter-specific artifacts (e.g., `.cpython-313.pyc`) are never committed.
#  */
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
wheels/

# /**
#  * Why: Isolate developer-specific Python virtual environments from the repository.
#  */
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# /**
#  * Why: Ignore local test runner, coverage, and static analysis caches generated
#  * by `pytest` and linter runs.
#  */
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/.adk/

# /**
#  * Why: `setenv.sh` writes active `PROJECT_ID` and `REGION` settings to `.env`, and
#  * developers may store GCP service account keys locally. Ignoring these prevents
#  * leaking environment-specific configuration or credentials while keeping `.env.example`.
#  */
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*service-account*.json
*credentials*.json

# /**
#  * Why: Terraform provider binaries and state files in `terraform/` contain large
#  * platform-specific binaries and potentially sensitive cloud resource state.
#  */
**/.terraform/*
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
.terraform.lock.hcl
crash.log
crash.*.log

# /**
#  * Why: `call_agent.py --save-image ./key_visual.png` writes a generated PNG to the
#  * workspace root during manual CLI testing; excluding it keeps the working tree clean.
#  */
/key_visual.png

# /**
#  * Why: Ignore operating system and IDE metadata files that vary across developer machines.
#  */
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

lab_instructions.md
